    "result_text": "The surefire test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), and compilation succeeds. The subsequent jacoco `check` failure (0.28 line coverage vs. an 0.85 gate) is pre-existing and structural: the project ships a single integration test that exercises only the owner-create path, so no change to this feature could reach 85% whole-app coverage. My new code is on the covered path. The audit line confirms correct output:\n\n```\nmemberId=NSW2716E6609E1\n```\n`NSW` (region from postcode 2000) + `27` (FY: 2026-09-01 \u2192 fiscal 2027) + `16E6609E` (upper-hex SHA-256 of telephone+lastName) + `1` (Luhn over `NSW2716E6609E`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe design keeps structural impact low by adding one small cohesive unit and routing everything through it, rather than growing any existing class:\n\n- **`OwnerMemberId.java` (new)** \u2014 the single home for the identity: `region(owner)` (postcode band \u2192 region) and `base(owner)` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, reusing `OwnerFiscalYear` and `OwnerCheckDigit.luhn`.\n- **`OwnerCustomerCodeAdvice`** \u2014 its assign method shrank to one line: `deduplicator.unique(OwnerMemberId.base(owner))`, so collision handling now applies to the memberId. (CC and body dropped; dead imports/field removed.)\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 dropped `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` mappings, added `memberId` (the stored, deduped value), and pointed `locality` at `OwnerMemberId.region`.\n- **`OwnerSegment`** \u2014 reads the region via `OwnerMemberId.region` instead of parsing the old dashed code.\n- **`OwnerAuditCreationAdvice`** \u2014 audit line now logs `memberId=` and dropped the membershipNumber computation.\n- **`OwnerCheckDigit`** \u2014 removed the now-unused `of(owner)`, kept the reused `luhn`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`/`checkDigit`/`membershipNumber` response fields with a single read-only `memberId`.\n\n`OwnerCreatedEventAdvice` needed no edit \u2014 it already reads the owner's primary identifier (now the memberId) and its Javadoc explicitly anticipated this unification. The `Owner` entity's `customerCode` column is retained as internal storage for the value (renaming it would touch a large class for no behavioural gain), while the exposed customerCode/membershipNumber/checkDigit fields are gone as specified.",
